You are a VERIFIER for one tech-debt finding in `/Users/david/projects/HiloAviation/hilo-figma-atos`. Confirm it against the ACTUAL code (open the referenced files with Read) — do not trust the finder.
Finding: {"title":"curriculumBuilder Inngest job never transitions to 'failed' on error — stuck 'building' forever","severity":"HIGH","area":"Background job reliability / state machine","files":["src/lib/inngest/functions/curriculumBuilder.ts","src/server/routes/routes-ai-curriculum-builder.ts"],"detail":"The `generate-curriculum` step (curriculumBuilder.ts:109-185) has no try/catch, and the function has `retries: 0` with no `onFailure` handler registered in functions/index.ts. If the Claude call throws (rate limit, API error), or `safeParseAIJson` throws, or the parsed JSON lacks `stages` (line 153-157 throws 'AI returned an invalid curriculum structure'), the DB row's `status` stays at 'building' (set at line 100) — it is never updated to 'failed'. The sibling file `curriculumEnricher.ts` (lines 193-209) demonstrates the correct pattern: wrap the risky step in try/catch, set `status: 'failed'` with an error message, then rethrow. `curriculumBuilder.ts` omits this entirely.","impact":"The client polls GET /ai-curriculum/build-status/:jobId expecting status to eventually become 'completed' or 'failed' (routes-ai-curriculum-builder.ts:651-655 doc comment). On any generation failure the job is stuck at 'building' indefinitely — the polling UI shows a perpetual progress spinner with no way to know the build failed, and DELETE /ai-curriculum/build/:jobId is the only way out (requires the user to notice and manually cancel).","recommendation":"Wrap the `generate-curriculum` step (and ideally the whole function body) in try/catch; on error, update `curriculumBuildJobs` to `status: 'failed', error: <message>` before rethrowing — mirroring the exact pattern already used in curriculumEnricher.ts.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

